# Browser assets `npm run build:all` builds: the framework bundles in Alis.Reactive.Assets/dist/
# (served as static web assets and packed into the NuGets), the sandbox's own bundles, and the
# sandbox's copy of the Syncfusion files it links (copy-vendor.mjs).
Alis.Reactive.Assets/dist/
Alis.Reactive.DesignSystem/dist/
Alis.Reactive.SandboxApp/Styles/alis-reactive.theme.css
Alis.Reactive.SandboxApp/wwwroot/vendor/
Alis.Reactive.SandboxApp/wwwroot/js/sandbox-plugins.js
Alis.Reactive.SandboxApp/wwwroot/js/sandbox-components.js
Alis.Reactive.SandboxApp/wwwroot/js/sandbox-components.css
Alis.Reactive.SandboxApp/wwwroot/css/sandbox.css

# On .NET Framework each AlisReactive package copies its browser assets into the
# web project's Content\{PackageId}\ after every build
# (build/AlisReactiveNetFrameworkContent.targets). The package is the source of
# truth; tracked copies only produce phantom diffs.
examples/net48-mvc-smoke/Content/AlisReactive*/
# The framework test app's components bundle, built by npm run build:all.
tests/Alis.Reactive.Framework.App/wwwroot/js/
# The example builds as an app outside this repository would (scripts/example.sh): the theme the
# design system copies into it, its stylesheet, its Syncfusion copy and the smoke's output.
examples/resident-intake/Styles/alis-reactive.theme.css
examples/resident-intake/wwwroot/css/app.css
examples/resident-intake/wwwroot/vendor/
examples/resident-intake/ci/app.log
examples/resident-intake/ci/smoke.png
